{"name":"Delta","hex":"#999b95","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Delta","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO, ICAO, ITU & IMO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the letter D.","Signal flag for the letter D."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Vespidae – certain potter wasps."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Delta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Delta (letter)","blocks":[{"text":"Delta is the fourth letter of the Greek alphabet. In the system of Greek numerals, it has a value of four. It was derived from the Phoenician letter dalet 𐤃. Letters that come from delta include the Latin D and the Cyrillic Д."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delta_(letter)"},{"title":"D","blocks":[{"text":"D is the fourth letter of the Latin alphabet, used in the modern English alphabet, the alphabets of other Western European languages and others worldwide. Its name in English is dee, plural dees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Latin_letter_D.svg/330px-Latin_letter_D.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/NAMA_Alphabet_grec.jpg/500px-NAMA_Alphabet_grec.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/NAMA_Alphabet_grec.jpg/1280px-NAMA_Alphabet_grec.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/NAMA_Alphabet_grec.jpg/500px-NAMA_Alphabet_grec.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The alphabet on a black figure vessel, with a D-shaped delta.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANAMA_Alphabet_grec.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo